IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdcsa-types`

-- Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001 — GOAL 2: THE CHILD DEVELOPMENT
-- CO-SAVINGS SCHEME (Part 2, ss 3-8).
--
--   "How much does the Government add to a child's account; who is the
--    trustee; are the moneys protected; where do they go on the member's
--    death; how may a wrong payment be recovered?"
--
-- The Scheme itself, its membership, caps and accounts, is made by
-- regulations under s 3, which are not in the source: a cap they set is an
-- input. Source: ../source/CDCSA2001.txt lines 328-567.

§ `Goal 2 — the co-savings scheme`

§§ `The co-savings arrangement (s 3(3))`

-- s 3(3): "an arrangement by which the Government makes contributions to the
-- bank account of a child eligible for that arrangement, equal to the
-- contributions made by or on behalf of any parent of the child". The most
-- the Government matches is for the regulations: an input, NOTHING if none
-- is given (then the encoding refuses rather than guess).
@ref s 3(3)
GIVEN eligible IS A BOOLEAN, `parent's contribution` IS A NUMBER, `cap remaining under the regulations` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Government's matching contribution, eligible:` eligible `, parent contributes` `parent's contribution` `, cap remaining` `cap remaining under the regulations` MEANS
    IF NOT eligible THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `cap remaining under the regulations`
         WHEN JUST cap THEN IF `parent's contribution` GREATER THAN cap THEN cap ELSE `parent's contribution`
         WHEN NOTHING  THEN REFUSE "the matching cap is set by regulations under s 3, which are not in the source"

§§ `Compulsory substitution of trustee (s 4)`

DECLARE `Trustee circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `(a) custody, care and control granted to the parent who is not the trustee`
    `(b) care and control granted to the parent who is not the trustee`
    `(c) custody, care and control, or care and control, granted to a non-parent`
    `(d) the member legally adopted`
    `(e) the trustee dead`
    `(f) the trustee lacks capacity`
    `(g) the trustee unable or unwilling for another reason`
    `(h) the parent trustee's substitution agreed by both parents`
    `(i) the non-parent trustee's substitution agreed by both parents and the trustee`
    `(j) the other parent satisfies a Director the parent trustee cannot act`

DECLARE `Incapacity substitutes` HAS
    `a donee of a lasting power of attorney with the authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a deputy appointed by the court with the power`           IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 4(1): "Unless otherwise provided in an order of court or directed by the
-- Minister, the trustee ... must — (a) ... be substituted with the parent to
-- whom custody, care and control has been granted; (b) ... the parent to whom
-- care and control has been granted ...; (c) ... the person granted custody,
-- care and control, or care and control ...; (d) ... the adopter ...;
-- (da) where the circumstances in paragraph (e), (f) or (g) exist ... and the
-- member has a legal guardian, be substituted with that legal guardian ...;
-- (e) ... the trustee's personal representative; (f) ... (i) a donee ...;
-- (ii) a deputy ...; or (iii) if there is no such donee or deputy, a person
-- nominated by the Minister; (g) ... (i) the person nominated by the trustee
-- and approved by the Minister ...; or (ii) if no person was nominated ..., a
-- person appointed by a Director ...; (h) ... a person whom both parents have
-- nominated ...; (i) ... a person whom both parents have nominated ...;
-- (j) ... B or a trustee nominated by B ... if a Director is satisfied".
-- s 4(2): the Minister may direct removal and substitution regardless.
@ref s 4(1)-(3)
GIVEN c IS A `Trustee circumstance`, `legal guardian` IS A BOOLEAN, inc IS AN `Incapacity substitutes`, `nominated and approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`the substitute trustee for` c `, the member has a legal guardian:` `legal guardian` `, incapacity substitutes` inc `, a nominee approved by the Minister:` `nominated and approved` MEANS
    IF `legal guardian` AND (c EQUALS `(e) the trustee dead` OR c EQUALS `(f) the trustee lacks capacity` OR c EQUALS `(g) the trustee unable or unwilling for another reason`)
    THEN "the member's legal guardian (s 4(1)(da))"
    ELSE CONSIDER c
         WHEN `(a) custody, care and control granted to the parent who is not the trustee` THEN "the parent granted custody, care and control"
         WHEN `(b) care and control granted to the parent who is not the trustee`          THEN "the parent granted care and control"
         WHEN `(c) custody, care and control, or care and control, granted to a non-parent` THEN "the person granted custody, care and control, or care and control"
         WHEN `(d) the member legally adopted`                                           THEN "the adopter"
         WHEN `(e) the trustee dead`                                                     THEN "the trustee's personal representative"
         WHEN `(f) the trustee lacks capacity` THEN
             BRANCH IF inc's `a donee of a lasting power of attorney with the authority` THEN "the donee of the lasting power of attorney"
                    IF inc's `a deputy appointed by the court with the power` THEN "the deputy appointed by the court"
                    OTHERWISE "a person nominated by the Minister"
         WHEN `(g) the trustee unable or unwilling for another reason` THEN
             IF `nominated and approved` THEN "the person nominated by the trustee and approved by the Minister"
             ELSE "a person appointed by a Director, until a nominee is approved"
         WHEN `(h) the parent trustee's substitution agreed by both parents`              THEN "the person both parents nominate"
         WHEN `(i) the non-parent trustee's substitution agreed by both parents and the trustee` THEN "the person both parents nominate"
         WHEN `(j) the other parent satisfies a Director the parent trustee cannot act`  THEN "the other parent, or a trustee the other parent nominates"

§§ `Protection of benefits (s 5)`

-- s 5: moneys paid in belong "to the member absolutely and — (a) the payment by
-- the parent does not constitute a 'matrimonial asset' ...; (b) ... does not
-- constitute a transaction at an undervalue or an unfair preference ..., or
-- form part of the estate of a parent who has been adjudicated bankrupt; and
-- (c) the moneys in the member's bank account are not assignable or liable to
-- be attached, sequestered or levied upon for or in respect of any debt or
-- claim".
@ref s 5
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`what s 5 says of moneys paid into a member's account` MEANS
    LIST "they belong to the member absolutely, from the date of payment"
         "a parent's payment is not a matrimonial asset under s 112 of the Women's Charter 1961"
         "a parent's payment is not a transaction at an undervalue or an unfair preference, nor part of a bankrupt parent's estate"
         "the moneys are not assignable and cannot be attached, sequestered or levied upon for any debt or claim"

§§ `Death of a member (s 6)`

-- s 6(1): the moneys "must be paid to the Public Trustee for disposal in
-- accordance with — (a) the Intestate Succession Act 1967, if the member was
-- not a Muslim at the time of death; or (b) section 112 of the Administration
-- of Muslim Law Act 1966, if the member was a Muslim". s 6(3): they do not
-- form part of the member's estate or answer for the member's debts.
@ref s 6(1)-(3)
GIVEN muslim IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
`the law the Public Trustee disposes of a deceased member's moneys under, a Muslim:` muslim MEANS
    IF muslim THEN "section 112 of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966"
    ELSE "the Intestate Succession Act 1967"

§§ `Recovery of a Government payment (s 8)`

DECLARE `Ground for recovery` IS ONE OF
    `(a) made in reliance on a false or misleading statement, document or information`
    `(b) made by reason of an error`
    `(c) utilised for purposes not authorised by the Scheme`
    `none`

-- s 8(1): on grounds (a)-(c) the Government may (d) recover from the
-- account; (e)-(f) set off against other Scheme or prescribed-scheme
-- payments; (g) recover from "the person in default" as a civil debt where
-- the payment was made on a false statement or an error caused or permitted by
-- that person; "(h) recover that payment from a parent or legal guardian of
-- the member as a civil debt, even if he or she is not the person in default
-- ..., if the Government is unable to recover that payment under paragraph (d)
-- or (g) or make the deduction or set-off under paragraph (e) or (f)".
-- s 8(2): the bank must not allow further withdrawals until the Government is
-- repaid.
@ref s 8(1)-(2)
GIVEN g IS A `Ground for recovery`, `a person in default` IS A BOOLEAN, `recovered by (d)-(g)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the means of recovery open to the Government, ground` g `, a person in default:` `a person in default` `, already recovered under (d)-(g):` `recovered by (d)-(g)` MEANS
    IF g EQUALS `none` THEN EMPTY
    ELSE append `(d)-(f)` (append `(g)` `(h)`)
    WHERE
        `(d)-(f)` MEANS LIST "(d) recover from the member's account", "(e) set off against other payments into the account", "(f) set off against payments to a parent under a prescribed scheme"
        `(g)` MEANS IF `a person in default` AND NOT g EQUALS `(c) utilised for purposes not authorised by the Scheme` THEN LIST "(g) recover from the person in default as a civil debt" ELSE EMPTY
        `(h)` MEANS IF NOT `recovered by (d)-(g)` THEN LIST "(h) recover from a parent or legal guardian as a civil debt" ELSE EMPTY

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

-- s 3(1)-(2): the power to establish the Scheme by regulations, and what they
-- may provide (offences up to $20,000 or 12 months, s 3(2)(j)); s 7: approved
-- persons by regulations; s 8(3): refunds by a trustee or approved person who
-- misuses the account.
@ref ss 3(1)-(2), 7, 8(3)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`Part 2 provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "s 3(1)-(2): the Minister may by regulations establish the Child Development Co-Savings Scheme and provide for membership, managing agents, contributions, payments, accounts, utilisation, transfers and offences (fine up to $20,000, imprisonment up to 12 months)"
         "s 7: the Minister may make regulations approving approved persons"
         "s 8(3): a trustee or approved person who utilises moneys for unauthorised purposes may be required to refund them, and co-savings contributions on moneys deposited to facilitate that may be recovered as a civil debt"
